[38;2;124;124;124mbounded on all of X (a Banach space, Baire) ⟹ ||T_n|| uniformly bounded. Here we[0m[38;2;124;124;124monly have pointwise bounded on A (closed convex ⊂ unit ball), and we conclude [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msup_{x∈A} ||T_n x|| uniformly bounded (weaker than ||T_n|| bounded). The proof [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mis a nice adaptation: Baire on A gives local boundedness, convexity propagates [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mto global boundedness on A.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNote: we cannot conclude ||T_n|| is uniformly bounded (that would need pointwise[0m[38;2;124;124;124mboundedness on all of X or a second-category set with interior in X). Indeed [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcounterexamples exist where ||T_n|| → ∞ but sup_{x∈A} ||T_n x|| bounded. E.g., [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mT_n = n·(coordinate n) on ℓ², A = {x : |x_n| ≤ 1/n²} ∩ ball, then ||T_n|| = n → [0m[38;2;124;124;124m∞ but sup_{x∈A} |T_n x| = n·1/n² = 1/n → 0. So the conclusion is genuinely about[0m[38;2;124;124;124msup over A, not operator norms. Good, consistent.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow let me also verify there's no answer leak in the problem. The problem text [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mis just the statement and constraints. No solution given. Good.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write up the proof cleanly.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mProof:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet g(x) = sup_{n} ||T_n x||. By hypothesis, g(x) < ∞ for every x ∈ A. For each [0m[38;2;124;124;124mM ∈ ℕ, define[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mK_M = ⋂_{n=1}^∞ {x ∈ X : ||T_n x|| ≤ M}.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mEach set {x : ||T_n x|| ≤ M} is closed (T_n continuous), so K_M is closed. The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mhypothesis gives A ⊂ ⋃_{M=1}^∞ K_M, i.e., A = ⋃_{M=1}^∞ (A ∩ K_M).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSince A is a closed subset of the Banach space X, A is a complete metric space, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mhence a Baire space. Each A ∩ K_M is closed in A. By the Baire Category Theorem,[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthere exists M₀ such that A ∩ K_{M₀} has nonempty interior in A. Thus there [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mexist a ∈ A and r > 0 such that[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mB_A(a, r) := {x ∈ A : ||x - a|| < r} ⊂ K_{M₀},[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mi.e., sup_n ||T_n x|| ≤ M₀ for all x ∈ B_A(a, r). In particular ||T_n a|| ≤ M₀ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfor all n.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow we propagate this bound to all of A using convexity. Let y ∈ A, y ≠ a. Set d[0m[38;2;124;124;124m= ||y - a|| (note d ≤ ||y|| + ||a|| ≤ 2 since A ⊂ unit ball).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf d < r, then y ∈ B_A(a, r), so sup_n ||T_n y|| ≤ M₀.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf d ≥ r, set t = r/(2d) ∈ (0, 1/2] ⊂ (0, 1) and z = (1 - t)a + ty. By convexity[0m[38;2;124;124;124mz ∈ A, and ||z - a|| = t d = r/2 < r, so z ∈ B_A(a, r), hence ||T_n z|| ≤ M₀ for[0m[38;2;124;124;124mall n. Now T_n z = (1 - t) T_n a + t T_n y, so[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mt ||T_n y|| = ||T_n z - (1 - t) T_n a|| ≤ ||T_n z|| + (1 - t)||T_n a|| ≤ M₀ + (1[0m[38;2;124;124;124m- t) M₀ = (2 - t) M₀.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThus ||T_n y|| ≤ (2 - t)M₀/t = (2/t - 1)M₀ ≤ (2/t)M₀ = (4d/r) M₀ ≤ (8/r) M₀[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(using t = r/(2d), so 2/t = 4d/r, and d ≤ 2).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCombining both cases:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124msup_{y ∈ A} sup_n ||T_n y|| ≤ max(M₀, 8M₀/r) < ∞.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore sup_{x ∈ A} ||T_n x|| is uniformly bounded in n. ∎[0m

